        "original_id": "6d7ec5f4-e9f8-5427-82df-fec4ab1faa7b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Home Rule League, Irish Parliamentary Party\n- Movements: Irish Home Rule movement\n- People: John Dunbar\n- Roles: Member of Parliament for New Ross\n- Events: New Ross by-election, 1878\n- Places: Ireland, New Ross, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland\n\nFacts:\n- The Irish Home Rule movement agitated for self-government for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League operated from 1873 to 1882 as a political party campaigning for home rule for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- John Dunbar was a Home Rule League politician who served as Member of Parliament for New Ross from February 1874 until his death in 1878.\n- The New Ross by-election in 1878 was held because the incumbent Home Rule Member of Parliament, John Dunbar, died.\n- The Irish Parliamentary Party replaced the Home Rule League.",
